Chromium 159.0.8154.4 -> 159.0.8154.7, for the 159.0.8154.4 tarball.

159.0.8154.7 is a tag on the 159 branch (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#106}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-12). It adds 95 branch commits to
159.0.8154.4 (#11), 31 of them not PGO/orderfile rolls or VERSION
increments: security fixes (zstd's allocations zero-initialized, the reverted
AudioContext SelfKeepAlive removal, Secure Payment Confirmation's request
ownership, PDFium page unload re-entrancy, the reverted subframe occlusion
tracking in WebUI, a Glic crash, and V8's ObjectCreateMap cache on global proxy
map migration, in the "Roll commits from side projects"), IndexedDB's fallback
backing store, enterprise reporting attribution, WebAuthn's Ambient UI mode,
WebUI toolbar and settings fixes, a native occlusion tracking revert.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/159.0.8154.4..159.0.8154.7 and the dependency whose DEPS revision
changed (V8), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations, CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule pointer
updates, DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime} and gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h;
commit 17fce321a22eb2ba726e9bb792ea9b8aa4770a9a, refs/branch-heads/8154@{#106}).
Skia's and Dawn's stamps and build/util/MINIBRANCH don't change.

Checked: applies to the 159.0.8154.4 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
159.0.8154.7; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or V8's DEPS revision); it adds, deletes and renames no files;
the 159.0.8154.4 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

